meta {
  name: Parties - Create
  type: http
  seq: 40
}

post {
  url: {{lego_data_service_base_url}}/api/v1/parties
  body: json
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  ~allowDuplicateName: true
}

body:json {
  {
    "partyType": "P",
    "partyFirstName": "Ann",
    "partyLastName": "Smith",
    "partyEmail": "ann@example.com",
    "partyCity": "Raleigh",
    "partyState": "NC",
    "partyCountry": "USA",
    "externalIdentities": [
      { "transactionPlatformName": "Bricklink", "externalPartyId": "annbricks" }
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  Adds a party and answers 201 with it. Use the returned partyId as fromPartyId on item intake.

  - partyType: P (person) or C (company). A company's name goes in partyFirstName.
  - Only partyType and a first or last name are required.
  - 409 with code DUPLICATE_PARTY: an existing party has the same email, external identity or name.
    Each error names the matching party id. Only a name match can be overridden: turn on
    allowDuplicateName.
}
